---
import { ArrowUpRight } from '@lucide/astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { catalog, formatDate, sitePath } from '../lib/catalog';
---
<BaseLayout title="Catalog health" description="How this community gallery collects sample metadata, preserves provenance, and treats known source issues.">
  <header class="page-heading container"><p class="eyebrow">Open source. Open about the details.</p><h1>A catalog you can<br />look behind.</h1><p class="page-lead">Original sources. Pinned revisions. Honest metadata. We keep the history visible instead of hiding the rough edges.</p></header>
  <section class="container page-content">
    <div class="metric-grid"><div class="metric-card"><strong>{catalog.totals.samples}</strong><span>Sample records</span></div><div class="metric-card"><strong>{catalog.totals.metadataFiles}</strong><span>Source metadata files</span></div><div class="metric-card"><strong>{catalog.totals.eligibleFolders - catalog.totals.missingMetadata}/{catalog.totals.eligibleFolders}</strong><span>Eligible folders with metadata</span></div><div class="metric-card"><strong>{catalog.sources.length}</strong><span>Original source repositories</span></div></div>
    <div class="wide-guide">
      <section class="content-panel"><h2>Collected from the source</h2><p>Last successful source snapshot: <strong>{formatDate(catalog.refreshedAt)}</strong> (<time datetime={catalog.refreshedAt}>{catalog.refreshedAt}</time>). Collection is configured daily at 04:17 UTC and can also be started manually. GitHub schedules are best-effort.</p><p>We read original sample metadata, not merged feeds that would duplicate samples. A source must be completely collected before the catalog can build. The sample code and contribution history remain in the original repositories.</p><div class="table-scroll"><table class="health-table"><caption class="sr-only">Source repositories and collected revisions</caption><thead><tr><th>Repository</th><th>Records</th><th>Revision</th></tr></thead><tbody>{catalog.sources.map((source) => <tr><td><a href={`https://github.com/${source.repository}`}>{source.repository}</a></td><td>{source.samples}</td><td><a href={`https://github.com/${source.repository}/commit/${source.commit}`}><code>{source.commit.slice(0, 10)}</code> <ArrowUpRight size={11} aria-hidden="true" /></a></td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></section>
      <section class="content-panel"><h2>Honest about the rough edges</h2><p>The collected source snapshot has <strong>{catalog.totals.errors} known errors</strong> and <strong>{catalog.totals.warnings.toLocaleString('en')} warnings</strong>. Existing reviewed findings are tracked separately from newly introduced errors, which block the refresh workflow.</p><p>Sample details show source metadata notes. A malformed or unverified declaration is not promoted into a promise of compatibility. Known missing preview paths use a clearly labeled generic image; failed image requests also recover to that same fallback.</p><p><strong>{catalog.totals.missingMetadata} eligible folder{catalog.totals.missingMetadata === 1 ? ' still needs' : 's still need'} source metadata.</strong> Undocumented sample records are not fabricated. Reviewed support-only directories remain inventoried but do not become standalone samples.</p><a class="guide-link" href="https://github.com/pnp/spfx/blob/main/sample-tracking.md">Read the remediation tracker <ArrowUpRight size={13} aria-hidden="true" /></a></section>
      <section class="content-panel"><h2>Pictures, prepared with care</h2><p>Primary screenshots are resized into cached, local WebP previews. Original source URLs and processing results remain available in the preview report. Animated originals use a representative still frame; the source repository keeps the full original media.</p><p>Images that are unavailable, exceed the build's safety limits, or cannot be decoded use the clearly labeled generic fallback. A placeholder is never presented as a screenshot of a real sample.</p><a class="guide-link" href={sitePath('/preview-report.json')}>View preview processing and provenance <ArrowUpRight size={13} aria-hidden="true" /></a></section>
      <section class="content-panel"><h2>What this does not verify</h2><p>Metadata validation is not a sample build, security certification or live demonstration. The central audit checks declared fields and exact repository asset paths. Preview preparation additionally fetches and decodes selected images; neither process proves screenshot relevance, all external link availability or runtime compatibility.</p><p>Before using a sample, read its documentation, review its permissions and validate it in your own development environment. The gallery does not conceal older samples simply because their versions are old.</p></section>
      <section class="content-panel"><h2>Take the data with you</h2><p>The normalized public catalog includes source revisions, honest quality notes and stable sample identities. It is generated from the same audited snapshot used to build these pages.</p><a class="guide-link" href={sitePath('/catalog.json')}>Explore the catalog JSON <ArrowUpRight size={13} aria-hidden="true" /></a></section>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
